  "final_message": "The bug was in `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py`. It converted `period_start` from seconds to milliseconds but compared usage timestamps against `period_end` still in seconds. Every record's millisecond timestamp was therefore far larger than the end bound, so all usage fell outside the period and billed as 0. I changed it to `end = to_millis(period_end)`.\n\nThe 24 existing tests pass. I did not add your reproducing test to the suite, so I haven't run it directly. `answer.json` is written with `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.",
